COMMON REAL DEFECT IN FOUR MODULES
Layout baseline is computed from rounded font ascent/descent with floor-distributed half-leading (bbt-ui/components.rs:620), and snapshots report it correctly. Paint passes a line-box origin at components.rs:2473; chrome/mod.rs:555-559 independently re-centres the padded mask using its height and rounds it. text.rs:379-385 uses ceil(descent*scale)+2 as the bitmap baseline, which is not the layout baseline. This can place actual ink a whole device pixel above OR below its measured baseline depending on font/line-height. This is NOT a global one-pixel offset: correcting every string in one direction would be wrong.
Proof from original pixels, no rendering/code change: text-shift-metrics.json searches only integer dx/dy in{-1,0,1} for each named captured text region. In many regions dy+-1 makes every RGB pixel exact (not just under the threshold), while the unchanged reported logical baseline is exact or within0.022px. Examples: documents rail/h0 774 bad->0 exact at dy-1; settings nav Appearance12.5px 375->0 exact at dy+1; graph title12px705->0 exact at dy+1 and log2/text11px1063->0 exact at dy-1; stream e0/ch-tab3/text10px190->0 exact at dy-1. Sign convention: compare web[y] against native[y+dy]. A probe shift is attribution, NOT a shipped correction or a new parity result. Identical translated glyph coverage rules out AA/weight/colour as the cause in those exact regions.

